  "live_records": {
    "q-53704": {
      "dom_id": "step-q53704",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Which of the following transformations map any polygon to a similar polygon?\n\nI. $(x,y)↦(y,x)$\n\nII. $(x,y)↦(x+2,y+1)$\n\nIII. $(x,y)↦(4x,4y)$",
      "worked_solution": "A similarity transformation is any transformation made up of rigid motions (rotations, reflections, and translations) and dilations. \n\nA similarity transformation will map any polygon to a similar polygon.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the transformations in turn.\n\n- Transformation I represents a reflection over the line $y=x.$ Thus, it is a rigid motion and, therefore, a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation II represents a translation by $2$ units to the right and $1$ unit upward. Thus, it is a rigid motion and, therefore, a similarity transformation.\n\n- Transformation III represents a dilation of scale factor $4$ and center $O.$ Thus, it is a similarity transformation.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
